  "content": {
    "title": "How to watch Texas vs Gonzaga: TV channel, time, live stream",
    "text": "Texas faces Gonzaga in a second-round March Madness matchup at Paycom Center.Ben Solomon/NCAA Photos via Getty ImagesThe Texas Longhorns are back on the court tomorrow, looking to keep their March Madness run alive, but they’ll have a tough test ahead against No. 3 seed Gonzaga. Texas has already taken the hard road to get here, first grinding out a two-point win over NC State in the First Four, then following it up with a solid 79-71 victory over BYU in the first round. After fighting their way into the tournament, the Longhorns have built some momentum at the right time.Gonzaga, as expected, handled business in its opener with a 73-64 win over Kennesaw State and now steps in as a 6.5-point favorite. The Bulldogs have the experience and consistency that make them a dangerous team this time of year, so Texas will need to bring its best effort on both ends of the floor. With a spot in the Sweet 16 on the line, the Longhorns have another opportunity to prove they belong and continue their tournament run.Texas will take on Gonzaga at 6:10 p.m. CST on Saturday, and fans across the country can tune in with Sling TV.When is Texas vs Gonzaga? What: Texas Longhorns vs Gonzaga Bulldogs — March Madness Second Round When: March 21, 2026, at 6:10 p.m. CST Where: Paycom Center, Oklahoma City, OK TV: TBS and truTV How to stream the Texas vs Gonzaga game without cableSaturday night’s Texas vs. Gonzaga game will air on both TBS and truTV, making it easy to tune in without cable. While all the top streaming platforms carry both networks, Sling TV is our top pick because it’s the most affordable. Sling Blue carries both channels and starts at just $45.99/month, making it more affordable than other popular platforms.But to lock in even more value during March Madness, you can upgrade to Sling Orange & Blue. While this won’t give you access to any extra games during the tournament, the package is currently half off your first month, meaning it costs as little as $29.99/month depending on your specific location. Here are all the ways you can stream March Madness with Sling: Sling TV 3-Month Prepay ($49.99 - $159.99/month then monthly recurring payments) Sling TV Blue (Starting at $45.99/month) Sling TV Orange & Blue (Starting at $60.99/month; half off your first month) If you don’t want to use Sling for any reason, you can catch the Texas vs Gonzaga game with any of these other streaming platforms as well: fuboTV ($48.99 for the first month, then $73.99/month with a 7-day free trial) DIRECTV STREAM ($89.99/month; there are no free trials right now for the base plan) Hulu + Live TV ($89.99/month with a 3-day free trial; also includes Disney+ and ESPN+) YouTube TV ($59.99/month for the first two months, then $82.99/month with a variable free trial)",
